part civ_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "CIV-1 · Property of spouses: community property from the marriage unless a contract sets separate property (.1); community is what either acquires during the marriage, earnings and the income of separate assets included (.2); separate is what a spouse owned before, acquires by inheritance or gift (unless given to both), or in exchange for separate assets (.3)."

source civ_1 "Civil and Family Code, CIV-1 Property of spouses (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version civ1_v1
  cite civ_1
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-03-01
  note "CIV-1 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-03-01; governs marriages from any date, from 2018-01-01."
